  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#40206\", \"PowerToys#33774\", \"PowerToys#10497\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before: making Keyboard Manager remappings depend on the active input method or language. #40206 asks for the same thing (activating a remap set only when a given input language is selected). #33774 was triaged by the team as 'KBM profiles mapped to IMEs'. The maintainer said it would be possible to auto-switch if the IME shift can be detected, and cross-referenced the profile-switching request #1881. #10497 asks for remapping by input mode and was left without a resolution. The feature is not implemented yet. Add a 👍 reaction to #40206 or #33774 to show interest. In the meantime, KBM mappings apply regardless of the input method, so you would have to enable or disable them manually, or use a third-party tool such as AutoHotkey.\"}",
